// Phase M6 robustness fixture: a `<Type>_<member>` name is INTERNAL (codegen still computes the mangled
// symbol), never a valid SURFACE identifier. A bare call to one — here `String_length(s)`, the internal mangle
// of `s.length()` — must hard-abort with no binary (call it as `s.length()` / `String::length`). Guards the member-
// table surface enforcement (rejectMangledSurface) against regressing to a silent bare-symbol call. Run under
// `--no-check` to hit that klower guard directly: with the checker on, `String_length` is now rejected a phase
// earlier as "unresolved name" (String's queries are real MEMBER methods, so the mangle is no longer a
// top-level symbol) — still rejected, still no binary, just caught by the checker first.
fun main(): Int {
  val s = "hi"
  return String_length(s)
}
